  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — the skewness of the lotteries — is not considered by the individual. The individual does not mention the probability mass on the zero outcome, nor does the individual refer to the distribution of outcomes in terms of favorable vs. unfavorable probabilities. The individual’s justification is based solely on the prize amount and the winning probability, not on the asymmetry of the distribution. The decision reason requires comparing the skewness (i.e., the proportion of probability on unfavorable outcomes), and specifically prefers the more right-skewed lottery (A). However, the individual does not consider skewness at all and instead focuses on the higher prize in A. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual’s reasoning is inconsistent with the decision reason’s rule, which would have led to preferring A due to greater right-skewness (more probability on 0), but the individual’s reasoning is based on prize size. Thus, the decision reason was not applied.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
